BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: a changed date that does NOT line up
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:with any date its series produced still inherits the two
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:things the series decides - whether it is private, and
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:whether it is cancelled.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:Why this file exists. A changed date that LINES UP with a
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:date of its series was already covered (see F5). A changed
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:date that does NOT line up is handled by a different piece
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:of code, and that piece passed the changed date to itself
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:as its own series, so the series' two flags were thrown
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:away. A PRIVATE pastoral series with one visit rearranged
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:onto another day therefore imported that visit as NOT
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:private, with its title, for everybody to see. Most
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:calendar programs do not repeat CLASS on a changed date,
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:because the standard does not ask them to, so the changed
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:blocks below deliberately say nothing about CLASS.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:Found by an outside review on 27 October 2026.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:(1) A PRIVATE Tuesday series, with a changed date moved to
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:a Wednesday the rule never produced. Both dates private.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:(2) A CANCELLED series, same shape. Both cancelled.
